From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Take the GPU rate and voltage
 from an OPP table

The GPU runs at 1008 MHz on 960 mV. The board pins the rate with
assigned-clock-rates, which the platform bus applies before the driver
probes, and the 960 mV sits on DCDC4 from the time the PMIC probes.
Nothing orders the two, and the driver cannot defer the rate.

Describe the point as an OPP table in the SoC dtsi, one row of
1008 MHz at 960 mV, the pair of the vendor firmware, and give the GPU
node the table. The board gives it the supply, DCDC4, and drops the
rates: the driver now sets the voltage and then the rate once at probe,
before the firmware reads it. The board keeps GPU0 on PLL_GPU0 as its
parent, as the core clock takes the rate from that PLL and must not pick
another parent. PLL_GPU0 is no longer listed in the assigned clocks.

DCDC4 keeps regulator-always-on and its fixed 960 mV window; the OPP core
requests the same voltage.

Not covered: more rows, which need the voltage of each point measured;
dropping regulator-always-on.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the GPU probes after
the PMIC, runs at the table's operating point, and its firmware boots.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 12 +++++++-----
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi   | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 62ca10cdf37b..2237d89662c8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -188,12 +188,14 @@ ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 
 &gpu {
 	/*
-	 * Fixed operating point: PLL_GPU0 at 1008 MHz (VCO 2016 MHz, P0 2)
-	 * with the core clock undivided, on VDD-GPU at 960 mV (DCDC4).
+	 * Fixed operating point from the OPP table: the driver sets VDD-GPU
+	 * (DCDC4) to 960 mV, then the core clock to 1008 MHz (PLL_GPU0 VCO
+	 * 2016 MHz, P0 2, core clock undivided). The core clock takes its
+	 * rate from PLL_GPU0, so the parent is chosen here.
 	 */
-	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU0>, <&ccu CLK_GPU0>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU0>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <1008000000>, <1008000000>;
+	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_GPU0>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU0>;
+	gpu-supply = <&reg_dcdc4>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index c1f2c042eb82..d95ccb60ee36 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -360,6 +360,21 @@ dsu_pmu: dsu-pmu {
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The GPU core runs at 1008 MHz on 960 mV, the pair of the vendor
+	 * firmware; the voltage is not measured on our boards. The GPU
+	 * firmware reads the clock once, so the driver sets this point at
+	 * probe and the table has no other row.
+	 */
+	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-1008000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1008000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000 960000 960000>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	/* 19.2, 24 or 26 MHz, set by the board */
 	osc: osc-clk {
 		#clock-cells = <0>;
@@ -409,6 +424,7 @@ gpu: gpu@1800000 {
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GPU0>;
 			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_GPU_TOP>;
 			power-domain-names = "a";
+			operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
